      "content": "Labor profiles vary widely across these regions, but Southeast Asia (Vietnam) generally offers a motivated, adaptable workforce suitable for assembly. Poland and Romania offer European-standard, highly skilled manufacturing pools, though labor costs are significantly higher than in Asia. For Nigeria and Kenya, the workforce is growing rapidly, but reliability for high-precision manufacturing may require more stringent initial training and oversight. Expect management styles in East Asia and SE Asia to be highly hierarchical, while European sites will likely be more process-driven.",
